Fixed the pi runner image shipping only the pi-acp bridge without the pi agent it spawns (ENOENT at session/new; image built green because build check + ACP initialize only exercise the bridge). Added generic AGENT_EXTRA_PACKAGES/AGENT_EXTRA_BINARY to the npm harness rather than a pi-specific hack, so any future bridge-style agent reuses it; AGENT_EXTRA_BINARY is asserted on PATH to catch this class of bug in CI. Kept pi-acp as AGENT_PACKAGE/AGENT_BINARY because that is the runtime ACP entrypoint (catalog command is [pi-acp]); the agent is the spawned dependency, so flipping them would verify the wrong binary. Did NOT touch binary/Dockerfile — probed its 4 runners (cursor/junie/kimi/mistral-vibe), all self-contained, no bridge. Verified: local build passes the new command -v pi gate; pi + pi-acp both on PATH; session/new reaches login instead of ENOENT. Pinned pi-coding-agent@0.82.0, verified working with pi-acp@0.0.31 in the built image.
